  "example_summary": "Computation of total income for partnership firm M/s. HIG with adjustments under Section 40(b), Section 40A(3), ICDS II, Section 32, and Section 72.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Partnership Taxation & Business Income\n\n| Area / Head | Statutory Section / Rule | Operative Threshold / Condition | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Partner Remuneration & Interest** | Section 40(b) | Authorization by partnership deed; slab-limits based on book profit | Excess salary or unauthorized interest disallowed; interest restricted to deed date |\n| **Current Account Interest** | Section 40(b)(iv) | Must be explicitly authorized by partnership deed | Interest on current accounts disallowed if deed specifies capital accounts only |\n| **Cash Payment Limits** | Section 40A(3) | Payments exceeding specified thresholds for stock-in-trade via non-electronic modes | 100% disallowance of expenditure incurred otherwise than by account payee instruments |\n| **Depreciation & Asset Ownership**| Section 32 | Assets owned and used for business purposes | Depreciation allowed even if registered in partner's name, subject to business user test |\n| **Brought Forward Losses** | Section 72 | Business losses of preceding assessment years | Set-off allowed against business income of current assessment year |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Section 40(b) Condition: Remuneration and interest to partners are deductible only if authorized by the partnership deed, and interest cannot be allowed for any period prior to the execution of the deed.\n\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Cash Payment Restrictions: Payments for stock-in-trade exceeding statutory cash limits through non-compliant modes attract total disallowance under Section 40A(3).",
